\begin{aligned}\iint_D x^{2} + y^{2}\,\mathrm dA & =\int_{0}^{2 \pi}\int_{3}^{5}((r\cos\theta)^2+(r\sin\theta)^2)\cdot r\,\mathrm d r\,\mathrm d \theta\\ & =\int_{0}^{2 \pi}\int_{3}^{5}r^{2}(\cos^2\theta+\sin^2\theta)\cdot r\,\mathrm d r\,\mathrm d \theta\\ & =\int_{0}^{2 \pi}\int_{3}^{5}r^{3}\,\mathrm d r\,\mathrm d \theta\\ & =\int_{0}^{2 \pi}\,\mathrm d \theta\cdot \int_{3}^{5}r^{3}\,\mathrm d r\\ & =2 \pi\cdot \int_{3}^{5}r^{3}\,\mathrm d r\\ & =2 \pi\cdot \frac{r^{4}}{4}\big|_{3}^{5}\\ & =2 \pi\cdot \left(\left(\frac{625}{4}\right)-\left(\frac{81}{4}\right)\right)\\ & =\frac{\pi}{2}\cdot \left((5)^{4}-\left((3)^{4}\right)\right)\\ & =\frac{\pi}{2}\cdot \left(625-\left(81\right)\right)\\ & =272 \pi.\end{aligned}
$$

